{"id":74498,"chebi_accession":"CHEBI:74498","name":"5-fluoroorotic acid","stars":3,"definition":"A pyrimidinemonocarboxylic that is orotic acid which is substituted by fluorine at position 5. It is used in yeast molecular genetics to detect expression of the URA3 gene, which encodes orotine-5'-monophosphate dicarboxylase. A yeast with and active URA3 gene converts 5-fluoroorotic acid to fluorodeoxyuridine, which is toxic to cells.","ascii_name":"5-fluoroorotic acid","names":{"SYNONYM":[{"name":"1,2,3,6-tetrahydro-2,6-dioxo-5-fluoro-4-pyrimidinecarboxylic acid","status":"C","type":"SYNONYM","source":"ChemIDplus","ascii_name":"1,2,3,6-tetrahydro-2,6-dioxo-5-fluoro-4-pyrimidinecarboxylic acid","adapted":true,"language_code":"en"},{"name":"5-fluoro-1,2,3,6-tetrahydro-2,6-dioxo-4-pyrimidinecarboxylic acid","status":"C","type":"SYNONYM","source":"ChEBI","ascii_name":"5-fluoro-1,2,3,6-tetrahydro-2,6-dioxo-4-pyrimidinecarboxylic acid","adapted":false,"language_code":"en"},{"name":"5-fluoro-6-carboxyuracil","status":"C","type":"SYNONYM","source":"ChEBI","ascii_name":"5-fluoro-6-carboxyuracil","adapted":false,"language_code":"en"},{"name":"5-fluorouracil-4-carboxylic acid","status":"C","type":"SYNONYM","source":"ChemIDplus","ascii_name":"5-fluorouracil-4-carboxylic acid","adapted":true,"language_code":"en"},{"name":"ENT-26398","status":"C","type":"SYNONYM","source":"ChemIDplus","ascii_name":"ENT-26398","adapted":false,"language_code":"en"},{"name":"FO","status":"C","type":"SYNONYM","source":"ChemIDplus","ascii_name":"FO","adapted":false,"language_code":"en"},{"name":"FOA","status":"C","type":"SYNONYM","source":"ChemIDplus","ascii_name":"FOA","adapted":false,"language_code":"en"},{"name":"NSC 31712","status":"C","type":"SYNONYM","source":"ChemIDplus","ascii_name":"NSC 31712","adapted":false,"language_code":"en"},{"name":"NSC-31712","status":"C","type":"SYNONYM","source":"ChEBI","ascii_name":"NSC-31712","adapted":false,"language_code":"en"},{"name":"Ro 2-9945","status":"C","typ